$Aeon::Books["Skill_Metl_z","cntnt"] = "So you wanna play with Metal huh? This is the skill of <f2>Metallurgy<f1>, or manipulating Metals. Metallurgy is an important skill that has been used in the advancement of technology throughout History! Now, the first step to Metallurgy will be obtaining some <f2>Explosives<f1>. You can purchase Explosives from the <f2>Central Market<f1> at one of the <f2>Terminals<f1>. First, you must find a suitable location to start <f2>Blasting<f1> for <f2>Ore<f1>. Ore is an unrefined compound usually consisting of Carbon and Metals, not worth much in itself, but Ore can be melted down to seperate the Metals to obtain the Metal you seek! Unlike '<f2>Aggriculture<f1>', Metallurgy is not an exact science, and even the most skilled often find themselves gambling for Ore. Blasting has a random chance of producing Ore, but the higher your level of Skill, the better chance you have of succeeding. In the Aeon world there are many Metals to be had, so to obtain the different Metals, one must use different <f2>Composite Charges<f1> to attempt obtaining more valuable Metals, using more precise Blasts! The different Charges are C-1, C-2, C-3, C-4, and C-5, all increasing in price and requiring more Skill to use! To attempt to Blast for some Ore, select the Explosive from your <f2>Inventory<f1> and click <f2>Use<f1> to toss the <f2>Primed Charge<f1>, and attempt to Blast some Ore out of the site! The Primed Charge will not start it's count-down until it has settled, so if you are quick enough you can even defuse and recollect your Explosive by grabbing it before it can settle! Once a Charge has settled, it will begin a Five second count-down, and then it will explode, attempting to Blast Ore from under the ground, if it succeeds, you will be notified with a '<f3>Success!<f1>' message. With no Metallurgy Skill, you will only be able to utilize C-1 Charges, which are limited to only Blasting for Lead. <f3>Harvesting the Ore:<f1> Once Ore has finished <f2>Crystallizing<f1>, one may notice a '<f2>Ripe-Spark<f1>' fire from the top of it, indicating that it can be harvested! To harvest your Ore, simply use your <f2>Construction Tool<f1> and uproot it... once you release it you can collect it like any other object. Some time after fully Crystallizing, the Ore will begin to <f2>Cluster<f1> off, and produce more crystallizing Ore, so it is best to be patient! One of the basics of learning Metallurgy, is learning how to read the progress of Crystallizing Ore, you can do this by <f2>Checking<f1> the Ore. You can Check Ore by binding the Metallurgy <f2>Skill Func<f1> to a key, if you don't know how, please refer to the Book '<f2>Key Binding<f1>'. That concludes the Introduction to Metallurgy! Please make sure you return this book before you are charged with a late fee!";
